# @see ADR-170 (multi-OS platform abstraction)
id: STYLE-015
title: Platform-specific system header included outside src/common/
category: style
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .c .cpp .cc .h .hpp
  exclude_paths: src/common/ vendor/ test/ tests/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: \#include\s*<mach-o/dyld\.h>
    message: "macOS-only header <mach-o/dyld.h> included outside src/common/ — belongs in platform_posix.cpp only (ADR-170)"
  - regex: \#include\s*<windows\.h>
    message: "Windows-only header <windows.h> included outside src/common/ — belongs in platform_win32.cpp only (ADR-170)"
  - regex: \#include\s*<direct\.h>
    message: "Windows-only header <direct.h> included outside src/common/ — use compat.h shims instead (ADR-170)"
  - regex: \#include\s*<process\.h>
    message: "Windows-only header <process.h> included outside src/common/ — wrap in compat.h (ADR-170)"
  - regex: \#include\s*<io\.h>
    message: "Windows-only header <io.h> included outside src/common/ — use compat.h shims (F_OK, access) instead (ADR-170)"
fix: "OS-specific headers belong in src/common/platform_posix.cpp (<mach-o/dyld.h>, POSIX headers) or src/common/platform_win32.cpp (<windows.h>, <direct.h>, <io.h>). Name shims (getcwd, popen) stay in src/common/compat.h. Business logic includes only platform.h and compat.h — never OS headers directly. See ADR-170."
